        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: துடைப்பம்",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "துடைப்பம் (tuṭaippam) — \"a broom\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Coconut ribs bound at one end, held short, swung low. It is the first thing that touches a வாசல் in the morning: the ground is swept, then wetted, and only then does the கோலம் go down on it."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Three houses, three words again — Kannada ಪೊರಕೆ (porake), Telugu చీపురు (cīpuru), Tamil துடைப்பம் (tuṭaippam). The doubled ப்ப in the middle is the one you have been holding since பெட்டி taught you to hold a letter twice."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Four."
