          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "சீப்பு (sīppu) — \"a comb\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A comb, and nothing borrowed about it. The ீ at the front is held long, and then the doubled ப்ப comes again, so it lands in the same shape as துடைப்பம் (tuṭaippam) and பெட்டி."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A சீப்பு (sīppu) and a மலர் are what go into hair on a morning that is being made something of, and the two turn up in the same sentence often enough to be worth learning together."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Five, and the run is closed: a needle, a rope, an umbrella, a broom, and a comb."
            }
          ]
        },
